#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""dsh-mud - loopback admin backend for the dsh-mu platform.

Serves a small JSON API that the gateway exposes at /admin/ after checking the
caller's platform session and role. It is deliberately *not* a second control
plane: every mutation goes through the same library the CLI uses
(`/usr/local/lib/dsh-mu/python/dshmuctl.py`), under the same state lock, so the
CLI and the admin UI can never disagree.

Trust model: binds loopback only, refuses non-loopback peers, and — when
/etc/dsh-mu/admin.token exists — requires the gateway to present it. AuthN/AuthZ
for browsers is the gateway's job (Lua session + role=admin).

Everything here is Python standard library only.
"""
